WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.060
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.900
Looking your best sometimes takes a bit of
effort, whether it’s a few hours shopping

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.760
for jeans that don’t make your legs look
like two toothpicks sticking out a watermelon,

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.610
or getting every single hair in its right
place.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.890
I know, your hair can be cruel sometimes.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:20.789
But putting blood, sweat and tears into our
appearance, sometimes very literally, is not

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:25.160
a new thing; mankind has been doing it for
thousands and thousands of years.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.430
Apes were barely out of the trees before they
started wondering if they’d look better

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:34.050
with banana skins over their nipples and a
few crocodile teeth through their ear lobes.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.609
So today we look at some of the most extreme
modifications that people have made to their

00:00:38.609 --> 00:00:44.530
own bodies.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:51.179
In Skee Lo’s famous love poem from 1995
he wrote “I wish I was a little bit taller,

00:00:51.179 --> 00:00:55.670
I wish I was a baller, I wish I had a girl
who looked good, I would call her”.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:01.079
And while the last two are possible, through
practice and Tinder, your height is something

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:04.309
you’re stuck with as it’s down to your
skeleton.

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:10.960
Stuff like boobs, noses and eyelids are changeable,
your skeleton is set though, isn’t it?

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.140
Well not as much as you’d think and if you
get to work on it early enough, you can put

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.990
in some serious interior design changes.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:25.659
Binding involves wrapping bandages or chords
very tightly around body parts for many months

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:30.100
and slowly changing the shape and alignment
of the bones.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.939
It’s normally done on infants as they are
much more malleable.

00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:39.979
The most extreme form is cranial deformation
or head binding, which has occurred all over

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:44.010
the world and is still does occasionally in
places like Polynesia and Congo.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:50.060
At birth, the skull is made up of 44 separate
bone elements, which are connected with tissues

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:55.219
called fontanelles, that allow the rapid brain
expansion that occurs at a young age.

00:01:55.219 --> 00:02:01.080
Over time, many of these 44 parts fuse together
but, surprisingly, the skull never actually

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.650
stops growing.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:07.420
Your cheekbones continuously draw back and
your forehead keeps pushing forward.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:10.530
That’s right, you’re getting a flat face.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:15.590
But before the fusing occurs, you can bind
up the skull and elongate it over a period

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:16.720
of months.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.430
In many cultures, such as the people of Tomman
Island, the practice is often done, since

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.980
a long head is associated with wisdom.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.910
For the Mayans it was thought to be aesthetically
pleasing.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:33.220
It’s also thought that some cultures were
trying to emulate other tribes who naturally

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:39.130
had this longer head since a mummified female
body found in Peru contained a fetus with

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:45.280
an elongated skull, meaning it must have been
genetic rather than caused artificially.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:50.900
In China, the practice of foot binding lasted
almost 1000 years, where young girls’ feet

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.640
were wrapped to make them as small as possible.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.569
It was thought to make them more attractive
and it saved them a fortune since they could

00:02:57.569 --> 00:03:00.390
buy their Converse from the kid’s section.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:03.920
Similar to binding is the practice of using
rings.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.360
The most famous, of course, are the neck rings
but it is a common misconception that you

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:12.780
are stretching the neck, somehow lengthening
the vertebrae.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:18.750
In fact, the weight of the rings acts to push
down the collar bone and the upper ribs, to

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.659
give the illusion of a longer, giraffe like
neck, but it is actually just shortening the

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:24.659
body.

00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:28.299
The practice still happens in some areas of
northern Thailand and Myanmar and parts of

00:03:28.299 --> 00:03:29.409
Africa.

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:34.720
The rings can end up weighing as much as 10
kilos and they either start at around 2 years

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.989
old, since it’s less painful to do it slowly
over time, or at age 12, when they are considered

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:41.200
ready to marry.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.680
I think they’ve been listening to too much
Beyonce; you don’t have to put a ring on

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:46.680
that.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.620
It’s not exactly sure how the practice started.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:54.129
Obviously it’s seen as elegant and beautiful
but some people also theorize that it was

00:03:54.129 --> 00:03:56.050
protection against tiger attack.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:04:00.629
It’s the same reason all British people
wear ankle bracelets, in case we are attacked

00:04:00.629 --> 00:04:03.980
by badgers, or is that just me?

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:10.159
As for the human bite, well it’s pretty
pathetic compared to many of our animal brethren.

00:04:10.159 --> 00:04:15.299
Although there are a surprising amount of
human bite attacks, over a thousand per year

00:04:15.299 --> 00:04:16.600
in New York alone.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:21.760
And if you want to add a bit more bite to
your bite, then it’s time for some extreme

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.450
dentistry.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:27.920
Teeth sharpening occurs in many pockets all
over the world, from the Congolese to parts

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.770
of Vietnam and South America.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.720
It’s often an aesthetic practice, done with
a chisel, but in Bali, teeth are thought to

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:40.280
represent negative emotions such as anger
and jealousy and so are filed down to lessen

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.920
this.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:47.720
For the Mayans it was a class based system
so a fancy set of sharp fangs was the equivalent

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.720
of some red trousers and a glass of pimms.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.950
Holes, we all have them and they are a source
of never ending hilarity and embarrassment.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:02.230
Most mammals have the same selection of orifices
as we do, except for a few types of mole which

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:10.830
have a thing called cloaca, which is one orifice
that has the combined use for excretion, urine

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.800
and reproduction; now that’s just disgusting.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:17.110
The cloaca is standard for all amphibians,
birds and reptiles though.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:23.090
Some mollusks have a thing called a siphon
which lets water, or occasionally air, flow

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:28.560
through, used for a combination of movement,
feeding, breathing and reproduction.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.720
I just hope they clean it between each one.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:37.080
But humans have a habit of creating artificial
holes which they then fill with piercings

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.390
or gradually expand using a series of rings.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:45.500
The ancient Egyptian King, Tutankhamun, is
one of the earliest recorded examples of ear

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:49.580
stretching since you can see it depicted on
his sarcophagus.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:55.680
The 5000 year old Ötzi the Iceman, who was
discovered in the Himalayas, also had flesh

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.680
tunnels.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:00.080
His My Chemical Romance t-shirt had unfortunately
not survived though.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:05.430
In some Hindu culture a woman’s nose was
pierced as a sign she was ready to be married.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:09.810
It was typically the left nostril too as that
was thought to relieve some of the pain of

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:10.810
childbirth.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:16.030
In ancient times, it would also help her attach
more jewelry to her face, which was important

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:22.450
since anything worn for the wedding was hers
to keep while everything else became her husbands,

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:27.810
so a chain between your nose and ear would
have been very handy for hanging diamonds,

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:30.182
car keys and the remote control.

00:06:30.182 --> 00:06:35.080
A quick mention too for the lip plate, popular
in East Africa and parts of the Amazon basin,

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.280
which normally involves a piercing in the
upper or lower lip and then a wooden disk

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:41.330
inserted to stretch it out.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:45.560
Actually, I could do with one of those at
Christmas, would make shoveling food into

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:47.130
my face so much easier.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:51.630
And finally, from dolphins on your ankles
to “this westerner is an idiot” written

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:54.790
in Japanese kanji, it’s the wonderful world
of tattooing.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:59.440
Various forms of tattooing have existed since
Neolithic times, perhaps even further back

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.850
but we don’t have direct evidence of it.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:07.120
Otzi the Iceman, who we mentioned before,
had tattoo markings to go along with his pierced

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:12.040
ears and his skin is the oldest example we
have found so far.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:17.670
There are wide ranges of reasons and designs
for tattoos, from the detailed full body tribal

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:23.310
images to markings on the arms and face, to
indicate a slave or perhaps a criminal.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:27.150
In Europe, tattooing was less common from
the middle of the second millennium but it

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:31.640
was reintroduced by Captain Cook and his crew
after a trip to Tahiti.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:36.680
The word Tattoo itself comes from the Tahitian
Tatau and many of Cook’s crew came back

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:41.630
with tattoos, which soon started a trend on
the high-seas and made them associated with

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.960
sailors and subsequently, the criminal classes.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:50.670
They still have a negative, criminal association
in places like Japan and are strongly discouraged

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:56.910
by many parts of the Islamic world, but around
45 million Americans have one or more tattoos

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.570
and a third of British people.

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:02.810
Making them extremely common, so, if you are
thinking of trying to rebel, you would actually

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:08.520
be better off getting a side parting, putting
on a sensible jumper and smoking a pipe.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:13.610
The rich history of body modification has
given us some weird and wonderful traditions

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:17.871
and let’s hope that some keep going, so
the entire planet doesn’t end up looking

00:08:17.871 --> 00:08:19.540
exactly the same.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:23.970
If you’re thinking about starting your own
cultural tradition, go ahead, but please call

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:28.530
you mum before you stick that thing through
there, I’m not sure it’s the best idea

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.470
you’ve ever had.

